{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Menus in Use",
  "summary": "Drag a menu's buttons, pin a menu open, make one stay open, and put a menu inside a menu.",
  "order": 5,
  "practice": "../_scenes/shape_cube_menu.blend",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1: Drag in the Menu",
      "text": [
        "1. Click Button 1 on the cube: its menu opens.",
        "2. Drag Round up and down: the cube rounds.",
        "3. Drag Twist left and right: it twists.",
        "",
        "Round and Twist were given their drags for you. Moving the mouse off the cube closes the menu."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "01_haul.mp4",
          "label": "In the viewport",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "operator": "kneady.drag",
          "with": {
            "target": "Cube",
            "region": 1,
            "button": 1
          },
          "moved": true
        },
        {
          "operator": "kneady.drag",
          "with": {
            "target": "Cube",
            "region": 1,
            "button": 2
          },
          "moved": true
        }
      ],
      "start": {
        "mode": "OBJECT",
        "select": [
          "Cube"
        ],
        "active": "Cube",
        "sidebar": "Kneady",
        "view": {
          "location": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            0.0
          ],
          "rotation": [
            0.71238,
            0.44106,
            0.28736,
            0.46412
          ],
          "distance": 10.0,
          "perspective": "PERSP"
        },
        "set": [
          {
            "path": "scene.kneady_on",
            "value": true
          },
          {
            "path": "objects[\"Cube\"].kneady.regions[0].tree_open",
            "value": false
          },
          {
            "path": "window_manager.kneady_row",
            "value": -1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2: Pin It with Shift",
      "text": [
        "1. Hold Shift and click Button 1: its menu opens, pinned.",
        "2. Move the mouse off the cube: the menu stays, and you can still drag its buttons.",
        "3. Press Esc to close it.",
        "",
        "A pinned menu stays wherever the mouse goes. Shift+click Button 1 again also unpins it."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "02_pin.mp4",
          "label": "In the viewport",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "operator": "kneady.close_menu"
        }
      ],
      "start": {
        "view": {
          "location": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            0.0
          ],
          "rotation": [
            0.71238,
            0.44106,
            0.28736,
            0.46412
          ],
          "distance": 10.0,
          "perspective": "PERSP"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3: Make It Stay Open",
      "text": [
        "1. In the Kneady tab, click the arrow beside Region 1, then click Button 1.",
        "2. Under Opens Menu, turn on Stays Open.",
        "3. Click Button 1 on the cube: its menu opens and stays, no Shift needed.",
        "4. Click in empty space to close it.",
        "",
        "Stays Open is for a menu you use a lot: one click keeps it up."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "03_stays_open.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "objects[\"Cube\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[0].menu_stays"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Cube\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[0].menu_stays",
          "is": true
        },
        {
          "operator": "kneady.click_off"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4: A Menu Inside a Menu",
      "text": [
        "1. Click Twist in the tree, under Button 1.",
        "2. Turn on its Opens Menu, and press Add to Its Menu.",
        "3. Click Button 1 on the cube, then click Twist: Twist's own menu opens, with its new button.",
        "4. Click Twist again to go back, and press Esc to close.",
        "",
        "A button in a menu can open one more menu. A drag on Twist still twists the cube."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "04_sub_menu.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "objects[\"Cube\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[2].opens_menu"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Cube\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[2].opens_menu",
          "is": true
        },
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Cube\"].kneady.regions[0].button_count",
          "at_least": 4
        },
        {
          "operator": "kneady.close_menu"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
